WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.125 --> 00:00:03.333
Each of your faces is
cause enough for celebration.

00:00:05.125 --> 00:00:06.166
You’re safe,

00:00:06.166 --> 00:00:07.416
you made it back,

00:00:07.416 --> 00:00:08.541
you made it home.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:12.875
We know in the books

00:00:13.708 --> 00:00:16.000
to a certain point how
the witchers were created.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.083
The reason we call it Blood Origin

00:00:18.083 --> 00:00:21.583
is because we're telling the tale
of the first prototype of a witcher.

00:00:21.583 --> 00:00:23.000
This witcher is not the witcher

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.458
we know who’s humanlike and,

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:30.458
you know, can take potions
and have powers.

00:00:30.458 --> 00:00:33.708
It's 1.0.

00:00:33.708 --> 00:00:35.041
But it's the origin

00:00:35.041 --> 00:00:38.125
of what enables witchers
to exist in The Witcher world

00:00:38.125 --> 00:00:39.625
in Sapkowski’s books.

00:00:39.625 --> 00:00:41.916
It’s wonderful and terrifying
at the same time

00:00:41.916 --> 00:00:45.875
because you want
to pay homage to the books

00:00:46.166 --> 00:00:49.541
and the lore and satisfy
all of those fans.

00:00:49.541 --> 00:00:53.166
But also, you want to
create a whole story

00:00:53.166 --> 00:00:56.875
that exists, that would
be worthy of a Sapkowski book,

00:00:58.125 --> 00:01:00.666
that lives on television
and is self contained.

00:01:01.083 --> 00:01:03.416
And getting to build that world

00:01:04.041 --> 00:01:07.333
and explain how everything

00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:11.125
came to be with The Witcher, it's
just, that's like a golden opportunity,

00:01:11.125 --> 00:01:12.583
couldn't get better than that.

